[# email/tracking-safe-cta: a button that adds UTM parameters to its link without breaking the URL.

   It appends utm_source, utm_medium, utm_campaign, utm_content and utm_term (whichever you pass) to the href,
   using ? or &amp; depending on whether the URL already has a query string, and placing them before any #anchor.
   When the href is a Klaviyo tag, whether it already contains a query string is only known at send time, so
   set `separator` to '?' (no query string yet) or '&' (already has one). The href itself, including Klaviyo
   tags, is left exactly as written. Klaviyo also rewrites links for click
   tracking, check your Klaviyo account's UTM and tracking settings so the two do not both add parameters.

   Compatibility
   - Outlook desktop: it is a content/button, see that component for Outlook limits (square corners).
   - Gmail apps: fine.
   - Dark mode: as content/button. #]
[% set parts = data.href.split('#') %]
[% set base = parts[0] %]
[% set hash = ('#' + parts[1]) if parts.length > 1 else '' %]
[% set query = [] %]
[% for key in ['source', 'medium', 'campaign', 'content', 'term'] %]
[% if data.utm[key] %][% set _ = query.push('utm_' + key + '=' + data.utm[key]) %][% endif %]
[% endfor %]
[% set joiner = ('&amp;' if s.separator == '&' else ('?' if s.separator == '?' else ('&amp;' if '?' in base else '?'))) %]
[% set tracked = base + (joiner + query.join('&amp;') if query.length else '') + hash %]
[[ c('content/button', { label: data.label, href: tracked }, { variant: s.buttonVariant, settings: { align: s.align } }) ]]
